The candidate patch modifies `lib/fetch/util.js` instead of `lib/fetch/headers.js`, targeting a different file than where the vulnerability exists. The gold patch fixes the `headerValueNormalize` function in `lib/fetch/headers.js` by replacing the ReDoS-vulnerable regex `/^[
	 ]+|[
	 ]+$/g` with a safe loop-based approach. The candidate patch modifies a different function in a different file, and its approach using `.trim()` (which trims standard whitespace, not just HTTP whitespace characters) followed by regex replacements doesn't match the spec-required behavior of only trimming HTTP whitespace bytes (, 
, 	, space). The vulnerability in `lib/fetch/headers.js` would remain unfixed.

